      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q16",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "def create_player(name, health=100, city=\"Vice City\"):\n    print(f\"{name} | HP: {health} | City: {city}\")\n\ncreate_player()",
      "options": [
        "It prints | HP: 100 | City: Vice City",
        "It prints None | HP: 100 | City: Vice City",
        "It stops with an error: name has no default, so the call has to pass it",
