    {
      "id": "q18",
      "text": "What is a keyword argument?",
      "options": [
        "An argument written with its parameter's name, like city=\"Liberty City\"",
        "An argument that has to be a word, not a number",
        "The first argument of a call",
        "An argument that changes the default for good"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q19",
      "text": "In the lesson, why give health and city default values?",
      "options": [
        "So create_player runs faster",
        "So the player can never change city",
        "So the same 100 and \"Vice City\" aren't written in almost every call",
        "Because a function can't have more than one parameter without a default"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q20",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "def total(price, tax=5):\n    return price + tax\n\nprint(total(20))\nprint(total(20, 0))",
      "options": ["25\n25", "25\n20", "20\n20", "25\n0"],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q21",
      "text": "After `create_player(\"Phil\", 50)`, what is city inside the function?",
      "options": [
        "50",
        "\"Vice City\"",
        "Nothing: city was not passed, so it has no value",
        "\"Phil\""
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q22",
      "text": "In `create_player(\"Phil\", 50)`, which parameter gets 50?",
      "options": [
        "city, since it is the one with a text default",
        "name, since it is the first one",
        "None: 50 is left over",
        "health, the second parameter, since 50 is the second argument"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q23",
      "text": "Which call prints `Lance | HP: 80 | City: Vice City`?",
      "options": [
        "create_player(\"Lance\")",
        "create_player(\"Lance\", 80)",
        "create_player(\"Lance\", city=80)",
        "create_player(80, \"Lance\")"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q24",
      "text": "A call passes a value for a parameter that has a default. What happens to the default?",
      "options": [
        "The passed value is used in its place, for that call only",
        "The default becomes the passed value for every later call",
        "The default is used and the passed value is ignored",
        "Python stops with an error"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q25",
      "text": "What does this print?",
      "code": "def f(a, b=10, c=20):\n    print(a, b, c)\n\nf(1, 2)",
